WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:10.000
Hatten sich die Menschen in Nahal Oz vor dem 7. Oktober daran gewöhnt, unter ständiger Bedrohung zu leben?

00:11.266 --> 00:12.833
Before October 7, yes.

00:13.000 --> 00:13.733
Yes,

00:13.733 --> 00:15.600
We got used to it.

00:15.600 --> 00:16.633
It was something,

00:17.000 --> 00:20.033
I cannot say "got used to it" because

00:20.033 --> 00:21.533
it always escalated,

00:22.066 --> 00:23.266
so every time you think,

00:23.266 --> 00:25.366
"Okay, this is the worst that can get."...

00:25.866 --> 00:27.100
At a certain point

00:27.100 --> 00:30.900
we realize that it always escalates.

00:30.900 --> 00:36.300
If you look at the years, let's say from 2000 to today,

00:36.466 --> 00:38.733
you will see the escalation

00:38.733 --> 00:40.266
very, very clearly,

00:40.266 --> 00:42.633
and it’s a very steep one.

00:43.466 --> 00:45.933
So I used to feel

00:46.000 --> 00:49.366
safe here because of all the means that I told you,

00:52.000 --> 00:56.200
and I even thought that it doesn’t matter...

00:57.633 --> 01:01.466
The logic of my head was that

01:01.466 --> 01:03.633
"Everywhere you go in Israel, there's terror."

01:05.033 --> 01:09.466
So, I either give up my rights to live where I was

01:09.466 --> 01:10.433
originated,

01:11.233 --> 01:15.700
or I accept it.
